       2/       0 :                     ; BlastEm-over-the-bus differential harness ROM (clean-room, authored here).
       3/       0 :                     ;
       4/       0 :                     ; Instrument only. BlastEm's `-D` GDB-remote stub halts the CPU at Init on
       5/       0 :                     ; entry; the RSP driver writes a RAM control block, sets breakpoints, and
       6/       0 :                     ; continues. The ROM dispatches per the control block and records observable
       7/       0 :                     ; side effects in work RAM. (PC/PC-register writes are unavailable over this
       8/       0 :                     ; stub, so all experiment selection flows through writable RAM.)
       9/       0 :                     ;
      10/       0 :                     ; Control block (driver writes before `c`):
